CellularResolutions -- A package for cellular resolutions of monomial ideals
****************************************************************************

Description
===========

This package aims to make working with cellular resolutions of monomial ideals
possible. Although the focus is on those constructs needed to work with
cellular resolutions, the package additionally provides basic functions to work
with cell complexes. For some direct ways to construct common cellular
resolutions for monomial ideals, see *note taylorComplex: taylorComplex, and
*note hullComplex: hullComplex,. Introductions to cellular resolutions can be
found in:

  * Ezra Miller (see https://services.math.duke.edu/~ezra/ ) and Bernd
    Sturmfels (see https://math.berkeley.edu/~bernd/ ), Combinatorial
    commutative algebra (see https://www.springer.com/gp/book/9780387223568 ),
    Graduate Texts in Mathematics 227, Springer-Verlag, New York, 2005. ISBN:
    0-387-22356-8
  * Dave Bayer (see https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dave_Bayer ), Ireena Peeva
    (see https://pi.math.cornell.edu/~irena/ ) and Bernd Sturmfels (see
    https://math.berkeley.edu/~bernd/ ), Monomial Resolutions (see
    https://dx.doi.org/10.4310/MRL.1998.v5.n1.a3 ), Mathematical Research
    Letters 5, pp. 31-46 (1998)
  * Dave Bayer (see https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dave_Bayer ) and Bernd
    Sturmfels (see https://math.berkeley.edu/~bernd/ ), Cellular resolutions of
    monomial modules (see https://doi.org/10.1515/crll.1998.083 ), Journal für
    die reine und angewandte Mathematik, vol. 1998, no. 502, 1998, pp. 123-140.

More generally, cell complexes can be constructed by creating cells using *note
newCell: newCell, or *note newSimplexCell: newSimplexCell,, and then the
maximal cells can be provided to *note cellComplex: cellComplex, to construct a
cell complex.

The example below follows Example 1.6 in Cellular resolutions of monomial
modules (see https://doi.org/10.1515/crll.1998.083 ), where two simplicial
complexes X and Y are constructed on the same monomial ideal. However, only X
supports a resolution.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = QQ[a,b,c, Degrees=>{{1,0,0},{0,1,0},{0,0,1}}];                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : v101 = newCell({},a*c)                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = Cell of dimension 0 with label a*c                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Cell                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : v012 = newCell({},b*c^2); v020 = newCell({},b^2); v210 =                |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|newCell({},a^2*b);                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : e112 = newCell({v101,v012})                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                         2                                   |
|o6 = Cell of dimension 1 with label a*b*c                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : Cell                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : e022 = newCell({v012,v020}); e220 = newCell({v020,v210}); e211 =        |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|newCell({v210,v101});                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : e121 = newCell({v101,v020});                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : f122 = newCell({e112,e022,e121})                                       |
|                                                                             |
|                                        2 2                                  |
|o11 = Cell of dimension 2 with label a*b c                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o11 : Cell                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : f221 = newCell({e220,e211,e121});                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : X = cellComplex(S,{f122,f221})                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o13 = X                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o13 : CellComplex                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : e212 = newCell({v210,v012}); f212 = newCell({e112,e211,e212}); f222 =  |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|newCell({e022,e220,e212});                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i17 : Y = cellComplex(S,{f212,f222})                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o17 = Y                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o17 : CellComplex                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i18 : prune HH X                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o18 = cokernel | ac b2 bc2 a2b |                                             |
|                                                                             |
|      -1                                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o18 : Complex                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i19 : prune HH Y                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o19 = cokernel | ac b2 bc2 a2b | <-- cokernel {1, 2, 1} | c a |              |
|                                                                             |
|      -1                             0                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o19 : Complex                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i20 : Y121 = subcomplex(Y,a*b^2*c)                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o20 = Y121                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o20 : CellComplex                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i21 : prune HH Y121                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|        1                                                                    |
|o21 = QQ                                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|      0                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o21 : Complex                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

