cellComplex -- create a cell complex
************************************

  * Usage: 
        cellComplex(R,maxCells)
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, that specifies the base ring for
        interpreting the labels
      * maxCells, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, that specifies the maximal
        cells for the complex
  * Outputs:
      * a *note cell complex: CellComplex,, 

Description
===========

The method cellComplex takes a ring R and a list of maximal cells and
constructs the corresponding cell complex. While the intent is for the supplied
cells to be maximal, including non-maximal cells is not forbidden and will
generate valid cell complexes.

The ring R is the ring over which the labels are interpreted. This function
does not directly check that the labels are in the correct ring.

+-------------------------------------+
|i1 : c = newCell {}                  |
|                                     |
|o1 = Cell of dimension 0 with label 1|
|                                     |
|o1 : Cell                            |
+-------------------------------------+
|i2 : C = cellComplex(QQ,{c});        |
+-------------------------------------+
|i3 : R = QQ[x,y];                    |
+-------------------------------------+
|i4 : C = cellComplex(R,{c});         |
+-------------------------------------+

