cellComplex(Ring,SimplicialComplex) -- Creates a cell complex from a given simplicial complex
*********************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note cellComplex: cellComplex,
  * Usage: 
        cellComplex(S,D)
  * Inputs:
      * S, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 
      * D, an *note abstract simplicial complex:
        (SimplicialComplexes)SimplicialComplex,, from which the cell complex is
        created
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Labels => a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, default value
        null, that maps simplices represented by monomials to labels
  * Outputs:
      * a *note cell complex: CellComplex,, that matches those of the given
        simplicial complex

Description
===========

This returns a cellular complex whose faces are those of the given simplicial
complex.

+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..f];                    |
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = monomialIdeal(a*f, b*d, c*e);|
|                                      |
|o2 : MonomialIdeal of R               |
+--------------------------------------+
|i3 : Delta = simplicialComplex I;     |
+--------------------------------------+
|i4 : C = cellComplex(QQ,Delta)        |
|                                      |
|o4 = C                                |
|                                      |
|o4 : CellComplex                      |
+--------------------------------------+

The optional parameter Label can be used to provide labels to the resulting
cell complex. By default all cells get a label of 1.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : S = QQ[x,y];                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : H = hashTable {a => x^5, b => y*x^4, c=>y^2*x^3, d => y^3*x^2, e =>     |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|y^4*x, f => x^5};                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : C = cellComplex(S,Delta,Labels=>H)                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = C                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : CellComplex                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : applyValues(cells C, l -> apply(l,cellLabel))                           |
|                                                                             |
|                      5   5   4    3 2   2 3     4                           |
|o8 = HashTable{0 => {x , x , x y, x y , x y , x*y }                          |
|                      5    5 2   5 3   5 4   4 2   4 4   5    3 3   5 2      |
|               1 => {x y, x y , x y , x y , x y , x y , x y, x y , x y ,     |
|                      5 2   5 4   5 3   5 4   5 2   5 4   5 3   5 4          |
|               2 => {x y , x y , x y , x y , x y , x y , x y , x y }         |
|                                                                             |
|o8 : HashTable                                                               |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                 }                                                           |
| 2 4   5 3   5 4                                                             |
|x y , x y , x y }                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

