complex(CellComplex) -- compute the cellular chain complex for a cell complex
*****************************************************************************

  * Function: *note complex: (Complexes)complex_lpList_rp,
  * Usage: 
        complex C
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note cell complex: CellComplex,, the cell complex for which to
        compute the chain complex
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Reduced => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value
        true, that controls whether the augmented chain complexes is used
      * Prune => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value
        true, that controls whether the modules in the chain complex are pruned
  * Outputs:
      * a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, the dimension of the complex

Description
===========

This constructs the cellular chain complex for a cell complex, taking into
account the labels on the cells. The resulting cell complex will be a complex
of modules over the ring associated to the cell complex. By default, the option
"Reduced" is set to true, so the resulting Complex has a rank 1 free module in
homological degree -1.

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x]                  |
|                                |
|o1 = R                          |
|                                |
|o1 : PolynomialRing             |
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : a = newSimplexCell({},x);  |
+--------------------------------+
|i3 : b1 = newCell {a,a};        |
+--------------------------------+
|i4 : b2 = newCell {a,a};        |
+--------------------------------+
|i5 : C = cellComplex(R,{b1,b2});|
+--------------------------------+
|i6 : complex C                  |
|                                |
|      1      1      2           |
|o6 = R  <-- R  <-- R            |
|                                |
|     -1     0      1            |
|                                |
|o6 : Complex                    |
+--------------------------------+
|i7 : complex(C,Reduced=>false)  |
|                                |
|      1      2                  |
|o7 = R  <-- R                   |
|                                |
|     0      1                   |
|                                |
|o7 : Complex                    |
+--------------------------------+

For details see Combinatorial Commutative Algebra Section 4.1. If we restrict
to the case of monomial labels, then, subject to some acyclicity conditions,
the resulting complex will be (up to a shift by 1 in homological degree) a
resolution of $S/I$ where $I$ is the ideal generated by the labels of the
vertices. With the "Reduced" option set to false, the resulting complex will be
a resolution of the ideal $I$ as a module.

+--------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : R = QQ[x,y,z];                               |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : I = ideal(x,y,z);                            |
|                                                  |
|o9 : Ideal of R                                   |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : vx = newSimplexCell({},x);                  |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : vy = newSimplexCell({},y);                  |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : vz = newSimplexCell({},z);                  |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : exy = newSimplexCell({vx,vy});              |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : exz = newSimplexCell({vx,vz});              |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i15 : eyz = newSimplexCell({vy,vz});              |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i16 : f = newSimplexCell({exy,exz,eyz});          |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i17 : C = cellComplex(R,{f});                     |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i18 : betti complex(C)[-1]                        |
|                                                  |
|             0 1 2 3                              |
|o18 = total: 1 3 3 1                              |
|          0: 1 3 3 1                              |
|                                                  |
|o18 : BettiTally                                  |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i19 : assert(betti complex(C)[-1] == betti res I);|
+--------------------------------------------------+

The option "Prune," also defaulted to true, controls whether the modules in the
complex are pruned before being returned. With the "Prune" option set to the
default of true, the resulting complex is visually nicer. However, unless the
labeling ring is fine graded, some of the structure will be lost.

+-------------------------------------------+
|i20 : R = QQ[x,y]                          |
|                                           |
|o20 = R                                    |
|                                           |
|o20 : PolynomialRing                       |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i21 : a = newSimplexCell({},x);            |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i22 : b = newSimplexCell({},y);            |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i23 : e = newCell {a,b};                   |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i24 : C = cellComplex(R,{e});              |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i25 : complex C                            |
|                                           |
|       1      2      1                     |
|o25 = R  <-- R  <-- R                      |
|                                           |
|      -1     0      1                      |
|                                           |
|o25 : Complex                              |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i26 : complex(C,Prune=>false)              |
|                                           |
|       1                                   |
|o26 = R  <-- image | x 0 | <-- image | xy ||
|                   | 0 y |                 |
|      -1                       1           |
|             0                             |
|                                           |
|o26 : Complex                              |
+-------------------------------------------+

