isFree(CellComplex) -- checks if the labels of a cell complex are free modules
******************************************************************************

  * Function: *note isFree: (Complexes)isFree_lpComplex_rp,
  * Usage: 
        isFree(CellComplex)
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note cell complex: CellComplex,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, true if all modules
        associated to the cell labels are free

Description
===========

This command checks if the modules associated to the labels in the cell complex
are all free, which is necessary for the complex to give a free resolution.

A monomial label always gives a free module, since the module for a monomial
label is the free module generated by that monomial.

Additionally, this function does not simply apply *note isFreeModule(Module):
(Macaulay2Doc)isFreeModule, to every label, as in general, the labels are given
as submodules, and so *note isFreeModule(Module): (Macaulay2Doc)isFreeModule,
would return false in nearly all cases. Instead the labels are first pruned
prior to calling *note isFreeModule(Module): (Macaulay2Doc)isFreeModule,.

+---------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z];              |
+---------------------------------+
|i2 : v1 = newCell({},ideal(x,y));|
+---------------------------------+
|i3 : C1 = cellComplex(R,{v1});   |
+---------------------------------+
|i4 : isFree C1                   |
|                                 |
|o4 = false                       |
+---------------------------------+
|i5 : v2 = newCell({},x*y);       |
+---------------------------------+
|i6 : C2 = cellComplex(R,{v2});   |
+---------------------------------+
|i7 : isFree C2                   |
|                                 |
|o7 = true                        |
+---------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note isFree(CellComplex): isFree_lpCellComplex_rp, -- checks if the labels
    of a cell complex are free modules
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in CellularResolutions/doc.m2:1017:0.

