texMath(CellComplex) -- Describes a cell complex or cell using TeX
******************************************************************

  * Function: *note texMath: (Macaulay2Doc)texMath,
  * Usage: 
        texMath C
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note cell complex: CellComplex, or a *note cell: Cell,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, 

Description
===========

This method functions mostly as *note net(CellComplex): net_lpCellComplex_rp,
and *note net(Cell): net_lpCellComplex_rp, does. The primary difference in the
output is that the output is formatted for TeX.

+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y];                                                     |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : v1 = newSimplexCell({},x);                                       |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : v2 = newSimplexCell({},y);                                       |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : e1 = newSimplexCell({v1,v2},x);                                  |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : e2 = newSimplexCell({v1,v2},y);                                  |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : f = newCell({(e1,1),(e2,-1)},x*y);                               |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : texMath cellComplex(R,{f})                                       |
|                                                                      |
|o7 = \textrm{Cell complex over }R\textrm{ of dimension }2\textrm{ with|
|     }5\textrm{ total cells }                                         |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : texMath f                                                        |
|                                                                      |
|o8 = \textrm{Cell of dimension }2\textrm{ with label }x\,y            |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : X = cellComplex(R,{f});                                          |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : texMath X                                                       |
|                                                                      |
|o10 = X                                                               |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+

